Subject: [PATCH] Release SYNC FrameData in SynchronizationLayer.channelRead

Upstream SynchronizationLayer.channelRead consumes each 0xFC SYNC
FrameData and returns without releasing it (only the derived ByteBuf
is released), tripping Netty paranoid leak detection once per received
SYNC. Mirrors MetricsSynchronizationHandler, which releases its
FrameData in the same situation. Tracked upstream; drop this patch
once upstream ships the fix.

Applies to upstream 76ab30a11a786daafb94c4ef95de457158cf80ce.
---
 .../raknetify/common/connection/SynchronizationLayer.java        | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/common/src/main/java/com/ishland/raknetify/common/connection/SynchronizationLayer.java b/common/src/main/java/com/ishland/raknetify/common/connection/SynchronizationLayer.java
index 4eec8dd..df6064d 100644
--- a/common/src/main/java/com/ishland/raknetify/common/connection/SynchronizationLayer.java
+++ b/common/src/main/java/com/ishland/raknetify/common/connection/SynchronizationLayer.java
@@ -200,6 +200,7 @@ public class SynchronizationLayer extends ChannelDuplexHandler {
                     FIELD_RELIABILITY_LAST_RECEIVED_SEQ_ID.set(this.reliabilityHandler, seqId);
                 } finally {
                     byteBuf.release();
+                    packet.release();
                 }
             }
             return;
